e. coverage of law enforcement from the investigation level up to court decisions on cases of Violence against Women and Children;
f. coverage of Women and Child Victims of Violence who receive legal aid services;
g. coverage of Repatriation services for Women and Child Victims of Violence;
h. coverage of social reintegration services for Women and Child Victims of Violence;
i. coverage of legal aid services from the Investigation level up to Court decisions for children in conflict with the law.

Article 6
Neglect as referred to in Article 2 letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of a child properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or other parties responsible for care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after a child as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts that neglect a person within the household scope, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obligated to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

